            {% set evs = nt_events(10, 7) %}{% if evs %}<style>.nt-events{margin:20px 0 4px;font-size:.85rem}.nt-events h6{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:.72rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;opacity:.65;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.15);padding-bottom:3px}.nt-ev{display:grid;grid-template-columns:78px minmax(160px,300px) 1fr;gap:10px;line-height:1.7}@media(max-width:700px){.nt-ev{grid-template-columns:64px 1fr}.nt-ev>span:last-child{grid-column:1/-1}}</style><div class="nt-events"><h6>Recent events &middot; <a href="/feed.xml">RSS / Atom feed</a> &middot; one tracker only: <code style="text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0">https://newtrackon.co.nz/feed.xml?tracker=example.org</code></h6>{% for e in evs %}<div class="nt-ev"><span><span data-nt-ts="{{ e.t }}"></span> ago</span><span>{{ e.host }}</span><span style="color:{{ {"down": "#ff3b30", "up": "#00e676", "good": "#00e676", "bad": "#ffa500", "family": "#ffa500"}.get(e.type, "#8ab4ff") }}">{{ e.text }}</span></div>{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}
<style>.nt-legend{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(250px,1fr));gap:10px 28px;margin:16px 0 24px;font-size:.85rem}.nt-lg h6{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:.72rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;opacity:.65;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.15);padding-bottom:3px}.nt-lg .r{display:grid;grid-template-columns:78px 1fr;align-items:center;line-height:1.7}.nt-lg .s{text-align:center;white-space:nowrap}</style><style>.nt-lg .r{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;margin:2px 0}.nt-lg .k{min-width:96px;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap}</style>
<div class="nt-legend">
<div class="nt-lg nt-lg-status"><h6>Status</h6>
<div class="r" title="Answering, passes every test, score 90+ (on the stable list)"><span class="k" style="color:#00e676">Up/Good &#11014;&#65038;</span>passes everything, 90+</div>
<div class="r" title="Averages 300 ms or more, or 200 ms or more with latency alone pulling its score under 90 (green if still 90+, orange below)"><span class="k" style="color:#00e676">Up/Slow &#128034;</span>healthy but slow</div>
<div class="r" title="Answering now, but score under 90 from recent misses"><span class="k" style="color:#ffa500">Up/Unreliable &#127922;</span>recent misses, under 90</div>
<div class="r" title="Healthy, under 7 days old: score capped while it builds history"><span class="k" style="color:#4fc3f7">Up/New &#128035;</span>under 7 days old</div>
<div class="r" title="Answering, but score under 50"><span class="k" style="color:#ffa500">Up/Junk &#128465;&#65039;</span>score under 50</div>
<div class="r" title="One published address family is dead; still works on the other. Score capped at 50"><span class="k" style="color:#ffa500">Up/Broken &#128148;</span>IPv4 or IPv6 dead</div>
<div class="r" title="Fails a quality test (hover the status for why)"><span class="k" style="color:#ffa500">Up/Bad &#128683;</span>fails a quality test</div>
<div class="r"><span class="k" style="color:#e0e0e0">Down &#129702;</span>not answering</div></div>
<div class="nt-lg"><h6>Latency</h6>
<div class="r" title="Average of the per-region medians; hover a latency for the breakdown"><span class="k" style="color:#00e676">green</span>under 200&nbsp;ms</div>
<div class="r"><span class="k" style="color:#ff9100">orange</span>200&ndash;299&nbsp;ms</div>
<div class="r" title="Penalty: &minus;0.02 per ms over 150 ms up to 1 s, steeper beyond (max &minus;40)"><span class="k" style="color:#ff3b30">red</span>300&nbsp;ms+</div></div>
<div class="nt-lg"><h6>Score</h6>
<div class="r" title="Score 0&ndash;100: availability &times; stability, minus penalties. New trackers are capped at 80, rising to 100 over 7 days"><span class="k" style="color:#f5c518">&#9733;</span>20 points each</div>
<div class="r" title="Up/New excepted"><span class="k" style="color:#8b93a1">Grey</span>under 90, not on the stable list</div></div>
<div class="nt-lg"><h6>Peer test</h6>
<div class="r" title="Hands our peer to a 2nd client"><span class="k" style="color:#00e676">&#10004;</span>passes</div>
<div class="r" title="Latest peer test failed"><span class="k" style="color:#ffa500">&#9888;</span>failed</div>
<div class="r"><span class="k" style="color:#ff3b30">&#9888;</span>failed 3 of 6: score 0</div></div>
<div class="nt-lg"><h6>Fake peers</h6>
<div class="r" title="Returned fake peers"><span class="k" style="color:#ffa500">&#9760;</span>fake peers</div>
<div class="r"><span class="k" style="color:#ff3b30">&#9760;</span>3&times; running: score 0</div></div>
<div class="nt-lg"><h6>IP families</h6>
<div class="r"><span class="k" style="color:#00e676">IPv4</span>works</div>
<div class="r" title="Published but dead for 3 checks"><span class="k" style="color:#ff3b30">IPv4</span>dead: score &le; 50</div>
<div class="r"><span class="k" style="color:#555">IPv6</span>not published</div></div>
<div class="nt-lg"><h6>Security shield</h6>
<div class="r" title="HTTP(S), or UDP that enforces the connection-ID handshake"><span class="k" style="color:#28a745"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="11" height="11" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 0 1.5 2.5v5c0 4 2.8 7.2 6.5 8.5 3.7-1.3 6.5-4.5 6.5-8.5v-5z"/></svg></span>spoof-proof</div>
